Z||000017||RiceCooker||10-13-2001||07:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Wolfhound:<BR><B>Good natured joking aside, Canada just sent 1/3 of it's Navy as support in the effort.<BR>The Canadian and U.S. Navy conduct joint exercises on a continuous basis to the point they are already fully integrated when the need arises.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Canada's navy is pretty weak but...<P>Canada and the U.S. do these combat navy simulations and so of course the us has this huge fleet of battleships and destroyers etc etc. While the canadians have a few destroyers, couple subs, etc. (No Battleships)<P>So what the Canadians did was group their destoyers in a line so it looked like a big battleship on the radar of the americans. So they knew that Canada had no battleships os they let this group of ships come right in between them and destroy most of the fleet. (In the simulation of course) <P>Always take your enemies seriously<P>||||reg||1
